# Cloudflare Workers static-assets exclusion list.
#
# wrangler.jsonc sets `assets.directory: "./"` — the repo root IS the document
# root, so WITHOUT this file every tracked file is published at
# https://big7construction.com/<path>. Verified live 2026-08-08: PENDING_MANUAL.md,
# TODO.md, DECISIONS.md, CLAUDE.md, AGENTS.md, tests/*.py, .env.example and
# .git/config all returned HTTP 200 on the client's production domain.
#
# The public surface is defined by the Dockerfile's explicit COPY list (the
# Railway/nginx fallback ships exactly those files and nothing else). This file
# makes the Cloudflare host of record match that surface. Anything not on the
# Dockerfile COPY list belongs here.
#
# `_headers` and `_redirects` are deliberately absent: Cloudflare consumes them
# rather than serving them (both verified 404 live), and excluding them risks
# the pipeline never reading them.
#
# Locked by tests/test_shipped_source.py — add a new non-public file to the repo
# and that test fails until the path is covered here.
#
# Syntax: .gitignore-style. Deny-list only, no `!` negations, because a
# negation cannot re-include a file whose parent directory is already excluded.

# ── Version control ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
# `.git/` is uploaded verbatim otherwise: .git/config leaks the private
# GitHub remote, .git/index leaks the full file inventory with blob SHAs.
.git/
.gitignore
.gitattributes
.github/

# ── Internal governance, planning, and session docs ──────────────────
# Every .md in this repo is internal. The only public document is the
# capability-statement PDF, which is not matched by these patterns.
*.md

# ── Tests, build tooling, and generators ─────────────────────────────
*.py
*.pyc
__pycache__/
.pytest_cache/
tests/
scripts/
Makefile
build.sh
build.bat
run.sh
run.bat
deploy-cf.bat

# ── Internal ADRs and postmortems (docs/big7-capability-statement.pdf
#    is deliberately NOT excluded — it is linked from the site) ────────
docs/adr/
docs/postmortems/

# ── Deploy + container config (describes our infrastructure) ─────────
Dockerfile
.dockerignore
nginx.conf
wrangler.jsonc
.railwayignore
.assetsignore

# ── Config that is build/test-time only, never fetched by the browser ─
site.config.json
LICENSE
.editorconfig
.env.example
.gitleaks.toml
.pre-commit-config.yaml

# ── Agent/automation state ───────────────────────────────────────────
.autoimprove/
.claims/

# ── Local dev cruft (never committed, but never publishable either) ──
# `.wrangler/` matters: a dry-run or local deploy leaves no-op-worker.js and
# other build artifacts there, and without this line the next `wrangler deploy`
# from a dev machine publishes them.
.wrangler/
node_modules/
.venv/
venv/
.idea/
.vscode/
.DS_Store
Thumbs.db
